# Automated workflow (Cursor must follow)

## Goal

Maximize automation: after a code change, the user should **not type PR title/body**. The only expected manual step is an intentional **“Merge pull request” click** (do not try to bypass branch protection).

One-shot runner standard (minimize RUN): for any multi-step operation, always create/update `tools/agent-run.ps1` and give the user exactly one command to run; never provide long sequences of terminal commands that require multiple RUN confirmations.

## Branch + commit discipline

- Always work on a new branch named `fix/...`, `style/...`, `chore/...` (never commit directly to `main`).
- Keep changes minimal and scoped to the requested goal.
- Commit messages use a conventional prefix: `fix: ...`, `style: ...`, `chore: ...`, `docs: ...`.

## PR creation (no manual text)

- Never open “compare” URLs or ask the user to copy/paste a PR body.
- PR title should come from the commit message.
- PR description must come from `.github/pull_request_template.md`.

Preferred PR creation methods:

1) **GitHub Desktop**: use “Preview Pull Request” → “Create Pull Request”.
2) If GitHub CLI is available: `gh pr create --fill` (auto title/body).

## Safety boundaries (do NOT do)

- Do not disable branch protection.
- Do not enable auto-merge that bypasses CI.
- Do not merge into `main` automatically.

